# Identifiability of Proper-Time Shear in D/H Absorption Systems

**Date**: 2026-07-06
**Status**: Gate -1 - NOT_YET_IDENTIFIABLE
**Purpose**: Define TEP proper-time observables that cannot be absorbed into velocity structure

---

## The Core Problem

For each absorber component (i), the observed velocity can be written as:

$$v_{\text{obs},i} = v_{\text{kin},i} + c \cdot \delta a_i$$

where:

$$\delta a_i = \ln A_i - \bar{\ln A}$$

The problem is that $v_{\text{kin},i}$ and $c \cdot \delta a_i$ are observationally degenerate unless $\delta a_i$ is predicted independently.

### Critical Rule

**A free component-level proper-time shift is not a TEP detection. It is just velocity fitting.**

TEP-BBN must not fit $\delta a_i$ freely. It must predict:

$$\delta a_i = \alpha g_i$$

where $g_i$ is fixed before fitting the D line.

